{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the R3 key-bound residual (checker 5b0fcc38, builder 003b5c6c): both options, as one follow-up.\n\nThe residual is not acceptable as permanent. Joining is a core path, and an outside caller with throwaway keys can refuse every newcomer for the rest of a run. The bound I set in 03e5f6d7 counted the wrong keys.\n\nRequest 31f98f33 (R3a) holds the fix. Keep the counted bound for keys that Membership grants standing, and hold denied reads outside that count. It starts with a read-only proposal, then adds a witness and one control. It also updates the threat-model residual paragraph, so D6 names whatever remains. If the fix proves larger than a phase 1 item, land the threat-model sentence alone first.\n\nR3 stays landed and deployed. This ruling places no hold on R3, BR-14 or any deploy. R3a runs as a parallel phase 1 lane beside BR-14, one gate at a time.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}